\title{CATEomics: Model Selection and Ensemble Learning in Heterogeneous Treatment Effect Estimation from High-Dimensional Omics Data}
\description{
Addresses the lack of a standardized and reproducible process for choosing among conditional average treatment effect (CATE) estimators in high-dimensional omics studies, where their estimation errors cannot be evaluated directly from observed outcomes. The package accepts a SummarizedExperiment, applies common preprocessing and data partitions across R and Python estimators, compares their out-of-fold estimates using proxy losses, supports model selection and ensembling, and returns the resulting CATE estimates to the original object for downstream omics analysis. Python backends are provisioned automatically through basilisk.
}
